---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const LAST_UPDATED = "October 12, 2026";
const DEVELOPER = "Artificial Igknorance";
const CONTACT_EMAIL = "info@artificialigknorance.com";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Artificial Igknorance">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12 px-4">

    <!-- Back link -->
    <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-accent hover:text-accent-deep transition-colors mb-8 text-sm">
      <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
      </svg>
      Back to Home
    </a>

    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-2 text-ink">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="text-muted text-sm mb-10">
      {DEVELOPER} &middot; Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}
    </p>

    <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none space-y-8">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">Our Privacy Commitment</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          All apps published by {DEVELOPER} are built with a privacy-first philosophy. We do not collect,
          store, or share your personal data. All information you enter into our apps (including your
          portfolio holdings, price alerts, health records, and settings) is stored exclusively on your
          device and never transmitted to our servers, with two exceptions: apps with an AI coaching or
          optional AI scanning feature send the relevant context, photo or file to a third-party AI provider
          solely to generate your response (Section 4), and apps with a free trial send a scrambled code so a
          trial cannot be restarted again and again (Section 3).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          We do not collect any personally identifiable information. Our apps do not require you to create
          an account or provide any personal details.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mt-3">
          The only data processed by our apps is:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-body space-y-2 mt-3 ml-4">
          <li>Market data (commodity prices, financial data) fetched from third-party APIs. These requests do not include any personal information.</li>
          <li>Anonymous crash and diagnostic data collected by Apple through standard iOS mechanisms if you have opted in to share analytics with app developers in your iOS Settings.</li>
          <li>For apps with an AI coaching feature, the context needed to generate your personalized plan (see Section 4).</li>
          <li>For apps with optional AI scanning, the photo or file you choose to scan (see Section 4).</li>
          <li>For apps with a free trial, a scrambled code that stops a trial being restarted (see Section 3).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">2. Data Stored on Your Device</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          All user-generated data is stored locally on your device using iOS secure storage. This includes
          your preferences, settings, portfolio holdings, price alerts, health records, and any other data
          you enter. This data stays on your device and is not accessible to us, apart from a photo or file you
          choose to run through AI scanning (Section 4).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">3. In-App Purchases, Subscriptions and Free Trials</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Where applicable, subscription purchases are processed entirely by Apple through the App Store.
          We do not have access to your payment information. Subscription status may be managed by
          RevenueCat, our subscription management platform. RevenueCat may collect a pseudonymous user
          identifier to manage your subscription state. No personally identifiable information is shared
          with RevenueCat. For more information, see
          <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-accent hover:text-accent-deep underline">RevenueCat's Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mt-3">
          Some apps that offer a free trial (for example, HealthTrail Medical) check that a trial has not
          already been used on the same device. To do this, the app sends our server a scrambled code (a
          one-way hash) made from an identifier Apple provides for your device, plus the app's name and the
          date your trial started. We keep those three items so a trial cannot be restarted again and again.
          The code cannot be turned back into the device identifier, and it is not connected to your name,
          your records, or anything else you enter in the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">4. AI Features</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Some of our apps (for example, Clock-In Everyday) include an AI-powered coaching feature. When you
          use it, relevant context needed to generate your personalized plan, such as your stated goals,
          equipment, injuries, freeform notes, recent workout history, and Apple Health-derived readiness
          metrics (e.g. sleep, heart rate, heart rate variability), is sent from your device to our
          Cloudflare Worker, which forwards it to Anthropic's Claude API to generate a response.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mt-3">
          This data is not tied to an account or any other identifying information, and our Worker does not
          store it. It is passed through solely to generate your plan and is not retained by us afterward.
          Anthropic's handling of this data is governed by
          <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-accent hover:text-accent-deep underline">Anthropic's Privacy Policy</a>.
          This feature is never used for anything beyond generating the coaching response you requested.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mt-6 mb-2">Optional AI scanning</h3>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Some of our apps let you scan something to fill in details for you: HealthTrail Medical (a photo of
          a pill bottle, insurance card, document or label) and SnapLedger (a photo of a bill, or a file you
          import). Scanning only happens when you choose it. When you do, the photo or file is sent from your
          device to our Cloudflare Worker, which forwards it to OpenAI's API to read the text. The details it
          finds come back to your device and are saved there.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mt-3">
          Our Worker does not store the photo, the file or the result, and none of it is tied to an account or
          your name. To limit abuse, the Worker counts requests from each network (IP) address, and that count
          expires after 24 hours. OpenAI says it does not use data sent through its API to train its models,
          and that it may keep API requests for up to 30 days to check for abuse. See
          <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-accent hover:text-accent-deep underline">OpenAI's API data controls</a> and
          <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-accent hover:text-accent-deep underline">OpenAI's Privacy Policy</a>.
          Scanning is never automatic, and every record it creates can be entered by hand instead.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">5. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Our apps may use the following third-party services depending on the app:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-body space-y-2 mt-3 ml-4">
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Gold-API.com</strong>: for live precious metal spot price data. Requests are made with an API key; no personal data is transmitted.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Yahoo Finance (public API)</strong>: for historical price and financial data. Standard HTTP requests are made; no personal data is transmitted.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">RevenueCat</strong>: for subscription management where applicable. See Section 3 above.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Anthropic (Claude)</strong>: for AI coaching features where applicable. See Section 4 above.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">OpenAI</strong>: for optional AI scanning where applicable. See Section 4 above.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Cloudflare</strong>: runs the secure relay that passes AI requests along and the free-trial check. See Sections 3 and 4 above.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Apple Push Notification Service</strong>: for local notifications. Notifications are scheduled locally on your device and do not pass through our servers.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">6. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Our apps are not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
          information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information through one
          of our apps, please contact us so we can address the issue.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">7. Data Security</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Because all user data is stored locally on your device, it is protected by your device's
          built-in security features, including device encryption and Face ID/Touch ID where applicable.
          We recommend keeping your device's operating system up to date to benefit from the latest
          security improvements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of material changes by
          updating the "Last updated" date at the top of this policy. Your continued use of our apps
          after changes are posted constitutes your acceptance of the revised policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">9. Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Since we do not collect or store your personal data on our servers, there is no personal data
          for us to provide, correct, or delete on your behalf. You can delete all locally stored app
          data at any time by uninstalling the app from your device. Data sent to an AI feature
          (Section 4) is not retained by us after your request is answered, so there is nothing to delete
          there. The scrambled free-trial code (Section 3) is not linked to you, but if you would like it
          removed, contact us and we will delete it.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mt-6 mb-2">If you are in Brazil (LGPD)</h3>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          Brazil's data protection law, the Lei Geral de Prote&ccedil;&atilde;o de Dados (LGPD), gives people in
          Brazil specific rights over their personal data. This part explains how our apps, including HealthTrail
          Medical, handle your data under that law.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mt-3">
          <strong class="text-ink">What we handle, and why.</strong> Your records, photos and backups stay on your
          own phone, and we cannot see them. The only things that reach us are a photo you choose to scan (for
          example a lab report, a medication label, or a health or insurance card) and, for apps with a free trial,
          the scrambled trial code described in Section 3. A health document can hold sensitive personal data, which
          the LGPD treats with extra care. We use a scanned photo for one purpose, reading it for you. Our legal
          basis is your consent, which you give when you choose to scan. Nothing is scanned unless you start it,
          and you can type every record in by hand instead.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mt-3">
          <strong class="text-ink">Where it goes.</strong> A scanned photo is sent to our Cloudflare Worker and on
          to OpenAI, which reads the text (Section 4). Both run outside Brazil, so scanning means your photo is
          transferred internationally. We do not keep the photo or the result. How long OpenAI keeps requests is
          described in Section 4.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mt-3">
          <strong class="text-ink">Your rights.</strong> Under the LGPD you can ask us to confirm whether we process
          your personal data, give you access to it, correct it, anonymize, block or delete data that is unnecessary
          or handled unlawfully, send it to you in a portable form, delete data we process with your consent, tell
          you who it has been shared with, and explain what happens if you say no. You can also withdraw your
          consent at any time. Because your records live only on your phone, you can already see, change and delete
          them yourself in the app, or by deleting the app. For anything we might hold about you, such as the
          scrambled trial code, write to us and we will answer.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mt-3">
          <strong class="text-ink">Who to contact.</strong> Send privacy requests under the LGPD to
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-accent hover:text-accent-deep underline">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
          That address is our point of contact for data protection (the <em>encarregado</em>). You also have the
          right to complain to Brazil's data protection authority, the ANPD (Autoridade Nacional de Prote&ccedil;&atilde;o
          de Dados).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">10. Contact Us</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed">
          If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us:
        </p>
        <div class="mt-3 p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-line">
          <p class="text-ink font-semibold">{DEVELOPER}</p>
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-accent hover:text-accent-deep transition-colors">
            {CONTACT_EMAIL}
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
